Z||000000||turbo86se||02-28-2000||03:44 PM||||<BR>hey everyone, it's time for my 88 coupe to get some new door hinges. They've been adjusted and adjusted and they still don't close right, or open evenly. Where is the best place to get them? Dealer? Fiero Store? Napa? Advance?  Are they easy to install? <P>I don't know if anyone will remember, but a week ago I posted a note about a parts car being delivered to my house so I could strip the interior. Well, that fell through but I did get my 84 parts car delivered unexpectedly to my house last week. I busted my butt removing almost every panel off the car, and the entire interior. Everything went well. A couple of my neighbors sat out on their front porch and watched me single-handedly strip the car. First the front fascia, then the fenders, next the doors (thanks for the tip, monkeyman! Good thing I had plenty of beer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) The Fiero is being towed out hopefully tomorrow morning. It doesn't have a cradle or rear wheels, it's just sitting there in front of my garage, blocking in my 86SE that's just begging to be driven in the 70's weather! If anyone wants it, LMK it's free! I do have the title. NOT THE 86SE!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  If anyone can bring a wrecker to Myrtle Beach, the stripped 84SE is yours!!!!!    -joel||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||02-28-2000||07:49 PM||||did you replace the pins and bushings? Did you try adding a nylon washer to the top half of the bottom hinge? The brass really doesn't support the vertical load worth a crud. too small. A single nylon washer fixes that perfectly. Without the nylon the 2 halfs of the bottom hinge tend to bind even with brand new bushings in. I use readily available nylon washers for sealing oil drain plugs. About a $1.50us for 3 of them.<P>You can adjust them? GM effectivly removed all the adjusting except for the front of the door moving in or out. I can't even move the damn strike pin. Unless you took the hinges off the A post and did some work to the post there's only a couple thousandths of play. Or did you shim the hinges on the door side like a couple others here have done?<P><B>WARNING</B><BR>Be Very carefull with the spring in the bottom hinge. If it gets loose it can and likely will hurt you. That spring compresses at around 75-100PSI per inch.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 02-28-2000).]||||reg||1
